  "topic": "Scoped Enum (enum class) in C++",
  "explanation": "In modern C++, 'enum class' introduces scoped enumerations that encapsulate enumerator names within a dedicated scope, preventing name collisions and improving type safety. Unlike traditional enums, enum classes do not implicitly convert to integers or other types, enforcing explicit conversions and reducing bugs. This feature enhances code clarity and maintainability by clearly associating enumerators with their enumeration type and avoiding polluting the global namespace.",
  "syntax": "enum class EnumName : UnderlyingType { Enumerator1, Enumerator2, ... };",
